  "query_preview": "..\n\nToday through next Friday...\n\nShower and thunderstorm chances will return Saturday through\nMonday. Southeast winds will advect in anomalously high PWAT\nvalues near 150% of normal. Saturday will have the best chance for\nthunderstorms with CAPE values up to 500 J/kg and 0-6 km shear\nvalues greater than 40 kts. Severe storms are not expected due to\nthe limited instability and weak upper level flow. \n\nSaturday night into Sunday will see a transition to more of a\nheavy rain threat due to moistening low levels (RH>70%) and \nweakening upper level flow. GFS soundings indicate LCL-EL cloud \nlayer wind speeds of less than 10 kts indicating slow moving\nstorms. Corfidi vectors will generally be above preferred values\nbut will briefly slow down to less than 15 kts increasing heavy\nrain potential. PWAT values of greater than 1 inch are near the\n90th percentile but forecasted soundings don't indicate the long\nskinny CAPE profiles that are ideal for heavy rain. Ensembles are\nindicating that precipitation will generally reamin below 0.75\ninches but 90th percentile values are in the 1-1.5 inch range east\nof Rosebud County. Locations from Rosebud County and west are\nexpected to receive significantly lower precipitation amounts. \nDue to this potential for heavy rain, WPC has issued a level 1 of\n4 risk for excessive rainfall for far southeast Montana. \n\nMonday will see an upper level wave move south from Canada\nbringing additional precipitation chances. Quieter conditions are\nthen expected to prevail through the rest of the workweek with\nonly minimal precipitation chances.\n\nTemperatures are expected to be in the 70s to low 80s F through \nTuesday. Temperatures then increase into the 80s F by Thursday. \nTorgerson",
